  "summary": "Traditional water-resistant hats crafted by Unangan (Aleut) people using bentwood techniques, featuring distinctive crests and waterproof design.",
  "description": "The aesthetic showcases curved forms with painted crests often depicting animals or spiritual symbols, constructed from multiple pieces of wood bent and sewn together with sinew, then waterproofed with seal oil. This design evolved from the practical need for waterproof headgear in the rainy Aleutian Islands while also serving as markers of identity and status within the community.",
